CVA6ConfigDcacheType = WT Signal Flow Tree (32KB 8-way Configuration)
=====================================================================

1. CONFIGURATION PHASE (cv32a6_imac_sv32_config_pkg.sv)
   └── localparam config_pkg::cache_type_t CVA6ConfigDcacheType = config_pkg::WT;
       └── cva6_cfg.'{ DCacheType: CVA6ConfigDcacheType }

2. BUILD/DERIVATION PHASE (build_config_pkg.sv)
   └── CVA6Cfg.DCacheType = config_pkg::WT
       └── cfg.DCacheType = CVA6Cfg.DCacheType;

3. MODULE INSTANTIATION PHASE
   └── std_cache_subsystem (core/cache_subsystem/std_cache_subsystem.sv)
       └── Cache type selection via generate blocks:
           ├── if (CVA6Cfg.DCacheType == config_pkg::WT) → Use WT cache ✓
           ├── if (CVA6Cfg.DCacheType == config_pkg::WB) → Use WB cache
           └── if (CVA6Cfg.DCacheType == config_pkg::WT_CLN) → Use WT_CLN cache

4. WT SPECIFIC INSTANTIATION
   └── wt_dcache (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache.sv)
       ├── wt_dcache_ctrl (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache_ctrl.sv)
       │   └── Cache controller for write-through policy
       ├── wt_dcache_mem (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache_mem.sv)
       │   └── Memory array without clean/dirty tracking
       ├── wt_dcache_wbuffer (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache_wbuffer.sv)
       │   └── Write buffer for write-through operations
       └── wt_axi_adapter (core/cache_subsystem/wt_axi_adapter.sv)
           └── AXI interface adapter for write-through operations

5. FUNCTIONAL IMPACT
   └── Write-Through Behavior:
       ├── All writes immediately propagate to memory
       ├── No dirty bit tracking required
       ├── Simplified coherency (no writeback logic)
       ├── Read hits serve directly from cache
       ├── Write hits update cache and write buffer simultaneously
       └── Write buffer provides write latency hiding

6. INTERFACE CONNECTIONS
   └── Cache controller interfaces:
       ├── CPU-side: req_ports_i/req_ports_o
       ├── Memory-side: axi_req_o/axi_resp_i
       ├── Write buffer interface for outstanding writes
       └── Bypass logic for uncacheable addresses

7. PERFORMANCE CHARACTERISTICS (32KB 8-way)
   └── Write-Through with 32KB capacity:
       ├── Larger cache reduces miss rate
       ├── 8-way associativity balances complexity vs hit rate
       ├── Write buffer absorbs write traffic
       ├── No writeback delays on evictions
       └── Predictable memory access patterns

KEY RELATIONSHIPS:
- DCacheType = WT selects standard write-through cache architecture
- Determines cache write policy and memory update behavior
- Write buffer critical for performance in WT mode
- No dirty bit overhead simplifies cache controller
- 32KB size provides good hit rates for typical workloads